@startuml
title Vault accounting: from a position to the tick bitmaps
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam DefaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FBFCFE
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}

package "Per user" {
  [Position PDA\nnft_id, tick, tick_id,\nsupply_amount, dust_debt] as pos
  [Position mint\n(SPL NFT)] as nft
}

package "Per vault" {
  [VaultConfig PDA\nCF, LT, LML, penalty,\noracle, rebalancer] as cfg
  [VaultState PDA\ntopmost_tick,\ncurrent_branch_id,\nexchange prices] as st
}

package "Tick space: -16383 .. 16383" {
  database "Tick PDA\nraw_debt, total_ids,\nis_liquidated, debt_factor" as tick
  database "TickIdLiquidation PDA" as tidl
  database "TickHasDebtArray PDA x16\n8 x 256 bits = 2048 ticks each" as bitmap
}

package "Liquidation history" {
  [Branch PDA\nminima_tick, debt_factor,\nconnected_branch_id] as br
}

nft -right-> pos : ownership proven by\nthe token account
pos --> tick : tick, tick_id
pos --> st
cfg --> st
tick --> bitmap : one bit set\nwhile debt is live
tick --> br : liquidation_branch_id
tick --> tidl : one entry per\nliquidation round
br --> br : connected_branch_id\n(merged chain)

note bottom of bitmap
  ratio = 1.0015^tick x 2^48.
  A tick encodes debt / collateral,
  so all positions in a tick share
  one health factor and liquidate
  together.
end note
@enduml
